{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana","id":934737,"title":"Space is the Murder Arcana","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-20T15:37:34-07:00","id":934737,"title":"Space is the Murder Arcana","content":"The Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 spell &quot;Secret Room&quot; is ridiculous. Observe:<br /> <br /> Maxine Mastigos is next to a nice suburban domicile where she <i>knows</i> a dinner party full of crooks is in full swing. This will not do.<br /> <br /> Now, she's your average Adept of Space - she has Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and Gnosis \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, so she has 3 Yantras available, a 1 hour ritual interval, and 8 dice to swing at this problem. She decides to give Secret Room a try.<br /> <br /> First, she spends her Reach to swap the Primary Factor to Potency - this gives her a base Potency of 4. She takes a -6 on the spellcasting dice pool to increase that to 7. She wants to encompass the first floor, so she needs to take another -6 to the pool - leaving her at -4! She decides to snip off a piece of a curtain (+2 material sympathy yantra), draws a few runes on it in Sharpie (+2 Runes yantra), and chants over it in a low voice (+2 High Speech yantra). At the end of the hour-long ritual, she touches the wall of the house.<br /> <br /> Immediately, the first floor compresses into a one-yard-radius sphere. Anyone who can't fit in that kind of space (which covers all of the crooks) gets pushed out of the bottom floor, taking 7L for their trouble. There is no Withstand. There's no real way to figure out <i>what the hell just happened</i> (most people are going to think explosion, not &quot;3 second spacial compression&quot;). Depending on whether or not the ST wants to consider walls and such &quot;subjects&quot; when you're casting it on a space containing multiple rooms, you can also make a case that you've <i>probably </i>destroyed something load-bearing, collapsing the building.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> The more I look at Space, the more <i>obviously</i> terrifying bullshit I see.<br /> <br /> Take, for example, Co-Location. You can roll Dexterity + Brawl to tap someone with your hand, then take a Reflexive action to swap them to the other location. Simples!<br /> <br /> Now, make yourself a soul stone, and put it somewhere actively threatening to life and limb. It's relatively cheap to get stuff into space (or <a href=\"http://sentintospace.com/\" target=\"_blank\">near space</a>). I hear space is <i>pretty</i> hostile to living creatures. Wrap an appropriate Ban around the soul stone, and it'll survive flying <i>into the sun</i> without problems.<br /> <br /> I <i>really</i> don't think I need to finish this train of thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T15:48:35-07:00","id":934743,"title":"","content":"This is true of every Arcanum. If you don't see the terrifying applications of an Arcanum, you don't really understand it very well.<br /> <br /> Edit: In your example, a Matter mage could liquefy the building for a turn, burying them in whatever the building is made from; a Mind mage could order them to kill themselves, a Life mage could make them deathly allergic to whatever they happen to be eating, Fate could cause them all to choke to death on their dinner at once, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 07-20-2016, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T15:53:58-07:00","id":934748,"title":"","content":"All Arcana are murder-arcana, trust me. All it takes is a minimal amount of thought, a small bit of malice and some time and then people are dropping left and right.<br /> My players even had a discussion about how to kill using the second dot, without doing direct damage. Every single arcana had one method or more, and that's just what they came up with on the spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T16:46:26-07:00","id":934777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana#post934737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, she spends her Reach to swap the Primary Factor to Potency - this gives her a base Potency of 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unrelated to your very truthful analysis of the lovely murder potential of Space, but I just realized I find it rather offputting how this needs to be done with Reach as opposed to just being a basic function of Creative Thaumaturgy in creating offshoots of the published spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-20-2016, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T17:23:12-07:00","id":934799,"title":"","content":"At level 3 or higher every single arcana can easily kill or remove a single adversary or a group of enemies from combat-<br /> Fate- arm wreck leg wreck blind and deaf with advanced reach for multiple targets<br /> Forces- lighting bolts striking multiple opponents with extra reach for knocked down and stunned , or u simply make them fly in the air with invert gravity<br /> Death- how about a massive soul removal ? Or is it better a rigor mortis that strikes an entire crowd at once?<br /> Life- paralysis, maiming or blinding or heart attack on a group of people<br /> Mind- u guys should really go kill ur selves <br /> Time - did that really happen? I don't think so. Lets do that again. (On time 4 or more, an entire group of people suddenly transform into babies)<br /> Prime- don't really know how to use this one honestly but should be something big and nasty full of mana leak<br /> Matter- u guys sure the air ur breathing in this room is oxygen?<br /> These are only very basic and stupid examples of mass damaging spells and possible effects, but I'm pretty sure other players on this forum came up with lots of ideas who might be worse. Not to mention, we're not even considering the possibilities of combining one or more arcana into one single spell, so for example a room is suddenly filled with plasma lava sparkling with radiation or the bodies of enemies get turned into stones with life and matter... etc.. etc..<br /> <br /> (Btw, i totally agree with u and think the space arcanum is simply devastating , I rank him among my top 3 broken arcana among time and mind.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","user":"Lasombra","date":". 07-20-2016, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T17:43:08-07:00","id":934817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana#post934737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Take, for example, Co-Location. You can roll Dexterity + Brawl to tap someone with your hand, then take a Reflexive action to swap them to the other location. Simples!<br /> <br /> Now, make yourself a soul stone, and put it somewhere actively threatening to life and limb. It's relatively cheap to get stuff into space (or <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://sentintospace.com/&amp;quot;]near</a> space[/URL]). I hear space is <i>pretty</i> hostile to living creatures. Wrap an appropriate Ban around the soul stone, and it'll survive flying <i>into the sun</i> without problems.<br /> <br /> I <i>really</i> don't think I need to finish this train of thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, using Space to send people to space is pretty poetic and fitting. ;p","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T18:10:09-07:00","id":934830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=934799#post934799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces- lighting bolts striking multiple opponents with extra reach for knocked down and stunned , or u simply make them fly in the air with invert gravity)</div> </div> </div> </div>With Forces 4 you can Pattern all energy in an area into heat, and then use Forces 3 to Perfect that heat into...<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'll let you finish that thought.<br /> <br /> (Also, put up a Friction Knife so the air flays them for the very sin of moving away from it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T21:12:51-07:00","id":934894,"title":"","content":"Space has always been the murder Arcana. Mastigos are scary, you guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T21:23:13-07:00","id":934901,"title":"","content":"Now try to figure out how to use your ~3 spell control slots to become relatively safe from being instant murdered when someone throw's a magical tantrum at you.<br /> [A good place to start is to get yourself a high potency Wards and Signs combined with Warding Gesture, and make a lot of Sworn Oaths with big duration that would be disturbed by you being, well, dead.]<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Why is Sworn Oath the ultimate antimagic safety belt? Because it will Clash of Will any supernatural effect that would prevent or hinder fulfilling your oath, be it by forcing you to do something, or by making doing something impossible. So, mind magic? Forced action, get out. Being bound in a Space Ban? Forced inaction, get out. Being stopped from being alive due to being scattered into small baby goats made of rust and cuddles? Forced inaction, get out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-21-2016, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T21:49:19-07:00","id":934907,"title":"","content":"BTW, why there are no traitors to Mysterium:<br /> <br /> 1. Hear that a Mysterium member Did Something Bad.<br /> 2. Ask your Egregore 5 dude with Space to punish that person.<br /> 3. Egregore dude gets into Mysterium Sanctum.<br /> 4. Instant Medium Sympathy to all Mysterium members! Yes, even you, Mister Traitor!<br /> 5. Instert any number of horrible things that can happen to you when someone with access to Space 3 has a Medium connection to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T23:19:15-07:00","id":934930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=934907#post934907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, why there are no traitors to Mysterium:<br /> <br /> 1. Hear that a Mysterium member Did Something Bad.<br /> 2. Ask your Egregore 5 dude with Space to punish that person.<br /> 3. Egregore dude gets into Mysterium Sanctum.<br /> 4. Instant Medium Sympathy to all Mysterium members! Yes, even you, Mister Traitor!<br /> 5. Instert any number of horrible things that can happen to you when someone with access to Space 3 has a Medium connection to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>BTW, why the Seers of the Throne won, are winning, and are doing victory jigs in their underwear.<br /> <br /> 1. Crown of Vision.<br /> <br /> Oh, I need to add more things to the list?<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> Also, Sworn Oaths + Conditional Duration has no drawbacks - just set the Oath to lapse <i>immediately</i> if you would accidentally break it.<br /> <br /> Hell, Fate 2 is a <i>wonderful</i> addition to the Mastigos Kill Room - a Conditional Duration that prevents your Co-Location + THE SUN trick from being used against you is <i>wonderful</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, Ban is an indestructible shield that can only be bypassed with Space. It blocks sensory range, deflects anything thrown at the boundary, and can be selective. So the first thing to develop is a version of Ban that moves with you...<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <b>The Bullshit That Is Ban</b><br /> What happens when your Ban only blocks Fate? The most obvious thing is that people outside it can't smack you with sensory range Fate spells - Fate can't pass the boundary, after all. Does this also block Destiny spending? Do you lose Hexes or Boons upon stepping through the boundary, regaining them as soon as you leave?<br /> <br /> Similar for stuff like Time - if I have a Ban against time up, is that area locked vs. time travellers fucking with the timeline?<br /> <br /> What if I allow Life but exclude Matter? Would people get blocked from entering due to the air in their lungs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T23:20:58-07:00","id":934931,"title":"","content":"Life 3 Fraying to damage cell regulation. You now have brain cancer.<br /> <br /> Pain and agony and misery and horror are <i>easy</i> with Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T23:27:34-07:00","id":934933,"title":"","content":"Ban can be bypassed by anything that fiddles with space, not necessarily Space. Acanthus can power their way out by Sworn Oathing, and you could probably cause timespace distortions by creating overlapping zone of slowed/accelerated time. Moros can use Touch of the Grave to reach into Twilight to tear their hole out. Thyrsus can manipulate Shadow and Twilight too. Obrimos...unless you consider influencing ley lines to create space-consequences, or consider manipulating gravity to cause space distortions, Obrimos are fucked.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Prime 3 probably can cut a hole through your Ban with Ephemeral Enchantment, as it, again, fucks with different worlds/phases of space. Wards and Signs might allow you to just walk out, and Bans are not going to be super-Potent spells, because 9 out of 10 effects that might contest Ban will do so using Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2<br /> And, in the end, you also have 3 other ways of escape:<br /> 1. Summon a Supernal Being. Act of summoning itself fucks with space.<br /> 2. Create a Soul Stone, then try to create a Demesne. Again, definitely fucks with space. \\<br /> 3. Start causing Paradox, hoping it will create a space-fucking paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-21-2016, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T01:09:35-07:00","id":934956,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't think sworn oath works that broadly as you think WHW. It forces a clash of wills if some supernatural power would change the actions of a subject, which has sworn the oath. So if you force somebody to go away from the door he swore to protect (action) or compell somebody to just watch while you break in (inaction), you get the clash of wills. So your examples for space and mind would work. Just outright killing somebody does not provoke a clash imho, since you don't force the subject to do or not do anything he wants. You simply take away the possibility to do anything at all. &quot;Inaction by death&quot; is kind of far fetched I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T03:16:16-07:00","id":934977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana#post934737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take, for example, Co-Location. You can roll Dexterity + Brawl to tap someone with your hand, then take a Reflexive action to swap them to the other location. Simples!</div> </div> </div> </div>Why am I reminded of the Bus Ticket, from The Lost Room?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T07:32:33-07:00","id":935053,"title":"","content":"The Lost Room, best 5 dollars I spent that month, if not that quarter xD God I love that series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T23:26:01-07:00","id":935464,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the one thing that Space has over the other arcana is advanced scale for a dram of mana at adept level instead of reaching.<br /> <br /> But otherwise, yeah, all the arcana are scary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T19:21:26-07:00","id":935894,"title":"","content":"I'd say space is more scary because the murder artist can be watching you at any or every moment and toss a spell from anywhere in creation at any time he feels like it.<br /> Sleeping? Contest this.<br /> In a trance of some sort? Enjoy.<br /> Sneaking around or facing off with some other enemy of yours? Let's make this a threesome!<br /> About to complete some long and difficult ritual? En garde!<br /> Diving into a swimming pool? Where did that active volcano come from?<br /> Getting dressed in the morning? Who put those scorpions in my pants?<br /> Driving somewhere? Who put that freight train an inch from my bumper?<br /> <br /> And the other guy can be on the moon or the bottom of the ocean while doing it. The only other Arcana that may be more broken in that respect is Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T23:12:06-07:00","id":936952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=935894#post935894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the other guy can be on the moon or the bottom of the ocean while doing it. The only other Arcana that may be more broken in that respect is Time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Spirit, where you hide on the other side of the Gauntlet (out of the reaches of Spaces magic) and send your legion of spirits to harass your foes.<br /> Or Death, where you hide in the underworld (out of the reaches of Spaces magic) and send your legion of ghosts to harass your foes.<br /> Or Mind, where you astral project into their psyche and murder their personality one idea at a time from the inside out.<br /> Or Fate, where you don't need to do anything at all but you've made arrangements that if in the future they do something you don't like that something bad will happen to eliminate them.<br /> Or Prime, where the small force of sleepers you've hired attacks them while warded against magic, wielding dissonance against obvious effects and carrying guns that you imbued.<br /> <br /> Wow... no wonder Mages are paranoid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:39:02-07:00","id":941904,"title":"","content":"Each of the Arcana is &quot;THE&quot; murder arcana.<br /> <br /> If any mage you run across doesn't have at least a dozen ways to kill you on tap, then they should feel bad.<br /> <br /> Which is why I tend to view conflict between mages as a proxy war. With mutually assured destruction more assured than a nuclear exchange, the mage community (at least in my mind) would tend to look for non direct routes for conflict resolution with other mages.<br /> <br /> It makes the consilium very important. Kind of like what the U.N. was supposed to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T10:07:18-07:00","id":942039,"title":"","content":"also remember that it takes a lifetime of practice to become an Adept at anything, it should take your PCs way more than one or two chronicles to get them at that level. If we\u00b4re talking about horrible arcana, than Fate takes the cake, forcing someone to live a life of misfortune is way worse than actually killing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","name":"BR_Malk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T10:14:00-07:00","id":942044,"title":"","content":"You can also start a chronicle with characters who are already masters if you feel that its an experience you are aiming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T10:24:27-07:00","id":942053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BR_Malk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=942039#post942039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also remember that it takes a lifetime of practice to become an Adept at anything, it should take your PCs way more than one or two chronicles to get them at that level. If we\u00b4re talking about horrible arcana, than Fate takes the cake, forcing someone to live a life of misfortune is way worse than actually killing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is personal opinion; don't state it as fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T10:35:37-07:00","id":942062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=941904#post941904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any mage you run across doesn't have at least a dozen ways to kill you on tap, then they should feel bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay... at this point I feel obligated to chime in and point out that not every human you encounter is a homicide waiting to happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Like, I totally agree with the &quot;every Arcana is pretty easy to come up with murder methods with&quot; sentiment, but this is taking it a bit too far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:44:29-07:00","id":942123,"title":"","content":"I thought the unspoken implication there wasn't &quot;they have a dozen ways to turn you inside out for looking at them funny&quot; so much as &quot;they have a dozen ways that they <i>can</i> kill you if they <i>need</i> to&quot;. Like, say, if you happen to be the sort of person who turns people inside-out for looking at you funny.<br /> <br /> Most non-PC Mages will never need to use the lethal application of their magic (although the implication that everyone <i>could</i> is a good way to make sure everyone stays civil), and even PC Mages can usually avoid it entirely if they're lucky and clever enough.<br /> <br /> I'm in a Mage game right now and the only people who've died in that were either victims of an industrial accident prior to the events of the chronicle, or death row inmates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","user":"Juhn","date":". 08-02-2016, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T05:24:30-07:00","id":943558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=942062#post942062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay... at this point I feel obligated to chime in and point out that not every human you encounter is a homicide waiting to happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Like, I totally agree with the &quot;every Arcana is pretty easy to come up with murder methods with&quot; sentiment, but this is taking it a bit too far.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Being capable, or even prepared to do something is vastly different than choosing or even wanting to do it.<br /> <br /> A mage making themselves aware of and capable of killing a being using the arcana at their disposal in no way equates to viewing everyone they run across as a target or a victim just waiting to happen.<br /> <br /> But knowing what dangers are out there, and then choosing not be prepared to deal with one when, not if, they are placed in mortal danger is bad decision making. And someone who so chooses should feel bad. If not for their own sake, then at least for those that they could have saved.<br /> <br /> One might even call it an act of hubris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T07:16:50-07:00","id":943604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=943558#post943558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage making themselves aware of and capable of killing a being using the Arcana at their disposal in no way equates to viewing everyone they run across as a target or a victim just waiting to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one step closer, mind. The moment where you realize on a fundamental, concrete and objective fashion of how frail life is next to your understanding of the universe, it makes taking that step all the more easier.<br /> <br /> It's something that I'd milk for personal horror. Particularly, after images of the killing imago whilst on mage sight. Should probably make a condition to portray this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T15:29:49-07:00","id":943935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=943604#post943604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The moment where you realize on a fundamental, concrete and objective fashion of how frail life is next to your understanding of the universe, it makes taking that step all the more easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T15:56:54-07:00","id":943958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=943935#post943935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok? Good for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T18:15:55-07:00","id":944035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=943604#post943604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's one step closer, mind. The moment where you realize on a fundamental, concrete and objective fashion of how frail life is next to your understanding of the universe, it makes taking that step all the more easier.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Or the more easily they can snuff out a life, the more likely they are to take safeguards to prevent wanton destruction. This I think is the crux of the wisdom mechanic.<br /> <br /> Just because you CAN do something, doesn't mean that you should. Being prepared for violence does not turn a mage into a murder hobo, degenerating down into the abyss.<br /> <br /> It is the tension of being ready to do what sometimes must be done to prevent greater horrors, while making every effort to avoid that necessity that brings out the best of this game line.<br /> <br /> But if sliding down into the darkness and reveling in carefree mayhem and death is your thing, more power to you.<br /> <br /> It takes all kinds, and there is no one right way to go about things in a game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T18:52:11-07:00","id":944061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=943958#post943958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok? Good for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know. I'm not going to bother supporting my opinion or anything. This is just one of those grey areas where you have an opinion, and I have a different opinion and we can agree to disagree. I just wanted to let you know the dissenting opinion was out there. No hard feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T23:32:12-07:00","id":944156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana#post934737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 spell &quot;Secret Room&quot; is ridiculous. Observe:<br /> <br /> Maxine Mastigos is next to a nice suburban domicile where she <i>knows</i> a dinner party full of crooks is in full swing. This will not do.<br /> <br /> Now, she's your average Adept of Space - she has Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and Gnosis \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, so she has 3 Yantras available, a 1 hour ritual interval, and 8 dice to swing at this problem. She decides to give Secret Room a try.<br /> <br /> First, she spends her Reach to swap the Primary Factor to Potency - this gives her a base Potency of 4. She takes a -6 on the spellcasting dice pool to increase that to 7. She wants to encompass the first floor, so she needs to take another -6 to the pool - leaving her at -4! She decides to snip off a piece of a curtain (+2 material sympathy yantra), draws a few runes on it in Sharpie (+2 Runes yantra), and chants over it in a low voice (+2 High Speech yantra). At the end of the hour-long ritual, she touches the wall of the house.<br /> <br /> Immediately, the first floor compresses into a one-yard-radius sphere. Anyone who can't fit in that kind of space (which covers all of the crooks) gets pushed out of the bottom floor, taking 7L for their trouble. There is no Withstand. There's no real way to figure out <i>what the hell just happened</i> (most people are going to think explosion, not &quot;3 second spacial compression&quot;). Depending on whether or not the ST wants to consider walls and such &quot;subjects&quot; when you're casting it on a space containing multiple rooms, you can also make a case that you've <i>probably </i>destroyed something load-bearing, collapsing the building.</div> </div> </div> </div>It will be really obvious if you compress a large space into a tiny space, in that things will be destroyed in a manner that is not consistent with the laws of physics. Not to mention, you can enjoy your rote paradox roll if any meaningful number of people are observing the space.<br /> <br /> Can you mass murder normies with vulgar magic? Yes. Should you? Not unless you're completely unafraid of paradox, Hunters, the Pentacle, the Seers, Banishers, Werewolves, Vampires, Demons, The God-Machine, Mummies, Changelings, many Spirit Choirs, and any other assorted supernatural who doesn't approve of mass murdering nutjobs who blatantly breach the veil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Meow! Meow meow meow. Purrrrrr.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","name":"Misterscruffles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T00:06:39-07:00","id":944167,"title":"","content":"Or losing Wisdom. That's not a very Wise thing to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T00:22:48-07:00","id":944173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=944035#post944035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the more easily they can snuff out a life, the more likely they are to take safeguards to prevent wanton destruction. This I think is the crux of the wisdom mechanic.<br /> <br /> Just because you CAN do something, doesn't mean that you should. Being prepared for violence does not turn a mage into a murder hobo, degenerating down into the abyss.<br /> <br /> It is the tension of being ready to do what sometimes must be done to prevent greater horrors, while making every effort to avoid that necessity that brings out the best of this game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I checked, the number of reported school shootings when the best firearm available was the musket was, I believe, null. Being prepared to snuff the life out of everyone in a room, brings you one step closer to finally doing so. Recognizing the option is what I mean. Besides, you probably know what they say about good intentions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T07:34:42-07:00","id":945451,"title":"","content":"I know the &quot;subtle&quot; and &quot;gross&quot; labels are really used for the Arcana anymore, but the old &quot;subtle&quot; Arcana are still great for, well, subtle kills. &quot;Acanthus hitman&quot; is a viable-like-whoa option, since Fate and Time can easily be used to turn you into &quot;the assassin who never misses his target&quot;: stop the target in their tracks with Time, enhance yourself with a Fate spell, take shot, collect bounty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T07:55:35-07:00","id":945459,"title":"","content":"Dude, it's fate. You don't need to take a shot. They'll just be stung by a bee which causes them to fall down the stairs and break a leg so that they have to go to the hospital which, on their way to, leads to them being in a rather fatal five car pile-up...<br /> Or whatever other horribly unfortunate scenario you can cook up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T08:21:50-07:00","id":945471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=945459#post945459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, it's fate. You don't need to take a shot. They'll just be stung by a bee which causes them to fall down the stairs and break a leg so that they have to go to the hospital which, on their way to, leads to them being in a rather fatal five car pile-up...<br /> Or whatever other horribly unfortunate scenario you can cook up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've once had an Acanthus kill a guy by throwing a lit cigar from a penthouse balcony. The victim happened to be driving by on a convertible, got distracted, crossed lanes, and had a head-on collision against a drunk driver going way above the speed limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T09:21:58-07:00","id":945492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BR_Malk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/934737-space-is-the-murder-arcana?p=942039#post942039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also remember that it takes a lifetime of practice to become an Adept at anything, it should take your PCs way more than one or two chronicles to get them at that level. If we\u00b4re talking about horrible arcana, than Fate takes the cake, forcing someone to live a life of misfortune is way worse than actually killing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Source? My book just says 4 XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T09:42:02-07:00","id":945502,"title":"","content":"First you need to get Gnosis 3, though, so it might be little more than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}